    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d141">

                <pb facs="0249" n="169" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg169"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-19"><hi rendition="#italic">May 19,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 990.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Continuing the subject-matter of my
                    dispatch No. 980, of the 8th instant, concerning the uprising in the southwest
                    of this province, I inclose copy of a letter from Rev. Mr. Houlding, who
                    recently came through the troubled district, and also of a note to our Chinese
                    secretary, Dr. Barchet, from the secretaries of the foreign office, to whom I
                    had sent him to inquire more particularly about the situation.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger</hi>.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d141-a1.xml" xpointer="d141-a1"/>
